<?php defined('BASEPATH') or exit('No direct script access allowed'); init_head(); ?><div id="wrapper"><div id="sc-enterprise-app"><div class="content"><div class="sc-enterprise-quicknav panel_s"><div class="panel-body" style="display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px"><a class="btn btn-default btn-sm" href="<?php echo admin_url('smart_choice_enterprise_core'); ?>"><?php echo _l('enterprise_dashboard'); ?></a><a class="btn btn-default btn-sm" href="<?php echo admin_url('smart_choice_enterprise_core/sales_operations'); ?>"><?php echo _l('enterprise_sales_operations'); ?></a><a class="btn btn-default btn-sm" href="<?php echo admin_url('smart_choice_enterprise_core/project_controls'); ?>"><?php echo _l('enterprise_project_controls'); ?></a><a class="btn btn-default btn-sm" href="<?php echo admin_url('smart_choice_enterprise_core/reporting'); ?>"><?php echo _l('enterprise_reporting'); ?></a><a class="btn btn-default btn-sm" href="<?php echo admin_url('smart_choice_enterprise_core/health'); ?>"><?php echo _l('system_health'); ?></a><a class="btn btn-info btn-sm" href="<?php echo admin_url('smart_choice_enterprise_core/help_guide'); ?>"><?php echo _l('enterprise_help_guide'); ?></a></div></div><h1><?php echo html_escape($title); ?></h1><p><?php echo _l('enterprise_help_intro'); ?></p><div class="row"><div class="col-md-6"><div class="panel_s" style="min-height:155px"><div class="panel-body"><h4>Dashboard</h4><p>Shows staff, enabled modules, queue jobs, audit records, and activity counts. The activity cards combine native Perfex and Enterprise Core tables. Example: a project created under Projects contributes to Project Controls.</p></div></div></div><div class="col-md-6"><div class="panel_s" style="min-height:155px"><div class="panel-body"><h4>Customer 360</h4><p>Find a customer, open their record, review contacts, projects, invoices and history. Customer properties and household details are entered in Customer 360; native invoices are entered in Sales &gt; Invoices.</p></div></div></div><div class="col-md-6"><div class="panel_s" style="min-height:155px"><div class="panel-body"><h4>Sales Operations</h4><p>Read invoices, estimates, proposals, contracts, projects and received payments from Perfex. Sales goals are entered in the Enterprise Core sales goals records if enabled. Example: record a customer payment against an invoice in native Perfex, then refresh Sales Operations.</p></div></div></div><div class="col-md-6"><div class="panel_s" style="min-height:155px"><div class="panel-body"><h4>Project Controls</h4><p>Shows native projects and tasks on the dashboard, plus Enterprise project phases, RFIs, submittals, permits and change orders. Create actual projects under Projects; use Enterprise tables for supplemental project-control records.</p></div></div></div><div class="col-md-6"><div class="panel_s" style="min-height:155px"><div class="panel-body"><h4>Reporting</h4><p>Summarizes native CRM records and Enterprise activity. Invoice totals and payments are separate measures; an invoice is not proof that a customer paid. Open native Payments and Invoices to reconcile figures.</p></div></div></div><div class="col-md-6"><div class="panel_s" style="min-height:155px"><div class="panel-body"><h4>Marketing</h4><p>Native leads contribute to the Marketing overview. Separate Marketing Project Tracker activity remains in its own module unless a dedicated integration is configured. Do not interpret an empty Enterprise campaign table as no marketing work.</p></div></div></div><div class="col-md-6"><div class="panel_s" style="min-height:155px"><div class="panel-body"><h4>Documents</h4><p>Native Perfex file records and Enterprise document versions/approvals are separate sources. Upload files through the appropriate native project, customer or document workflow.</p></div></div></div><div class="col-md-6"><div class="panel_s" style="min-height:155px"><div class="panel-body"><h4>Field Operations and Dispatch</h4><p>Track field visits, time logs, daily logs, and dispatch assignments in their Enterprise sections. Assign work to a staff member and project where the form supports it.</p></div></div></div><div class="col-md-6"><div class="panel_s" style="min-height:155px"><div class="panel-body"><h4>Equipment and Inventory</h4><p>Maintain equipment, inventory items and movements in the corresponding Enterprise records. Entries are separate from native invoice line items.</p></div></div></div><div class="col-md-6"><div class="panel_s" style="min-height:155px"><div class="panel-body"><h4>Communications and Call Center</h4><p>Review communication logs and call activity. Call tracking depends on correctly configured integrations and actual logged records.</p></div></div></div><div class="col-md-6"><div class="panel_s" style="min-height:155px"><div class="panel-body"><h4>Workflows, Queue and Feature Flags</h4><p>Queue jobs are Enterprise background tasks, not all CRM tasks. Enable features intentionally; review failed jobs and logs. A zero queue count can be normal.</p></div></div></div><div class="col-md-6"><div class="panel_s" style="min-height:155px"><div class="panel-body"><h4>Security, Audit and Permissions</h4><p>Staff roles control page access. Field rules are supplementary and do not override native Perfex security. Audit count reflects Enterprise Core audit events, not every action in Perfex.</p></div></div></div><div class="col-md-6"><div class="panel_s" style="min-height:155px"><div class="panel-body"><h4>System Health</h4><p>Checks runtime, writable directories, cron status and module tables. Action Required identifies a failed check; PHP version targets should be interpreted as compatibility checks, not automatic evidence of an error.</p></div></div></div><div class="col-md-6"><div class="panel_s" style="min-height:155px"><div class="panel-body"><h4>Getting started</h4><p>1. Open Dashboard to review the summary. 2. Create or review a native customer, project and invoice. 3. Record a payment through Perfex. 4. Refresh Sales Operations and Reports. 5. Review System Health. 6. Grant staff only the permissions they need.</p></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><?php init_tail(); ?>